{"author":{"id":"b409816c5cd5ab140d1d52eb33aace35de44952bb794b19806fd57f6ecb1ace9"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1790342643,"nonce":"bsK2etAeTbNJfD3gKZYan0Ohty8=","title":"compute(): @device, @workgroup and @kernel(x) modifiers are parsed and never read","message":"The zyn_peg interpreter builds TypedComputeExpr with every annotation as a modifier and copies `kernel` and `workgroup` into kernel_attrs (crates/zyn_peg/src/runtime2/interpreter.rs). No compiler pass reads `modifiers` or `kernel_attrs`; extract_kernel_type only looks at the in-body `@kernel name` sentinel. `@device(\"metal\")` therefore produces CPU SIMD code, and `compute(A, B) @kernel(matmul) @workgroup(16, 16)` becomes a Generic dispatch.\n\nThe type checker returns a fresh type variable for TypedExpression::Compute, so kernel bodies are not type checked either.\n\nWanted: lowering reads the modifiers; an unknown device or kernel kind is a compile error.","files":null}]}